# =============================================================================
# The build context (W1-1): the whole tree, but what must never be in an
# image. The test stage copies the context entire -- the suite reads tests/,
# deploy/, scripts/, .github/, the *.md files, this file and .gitignore --
# and the runtime stage copies a white list of it (Dockerfile), so weight
# and stray files stay out of the image the service runs by its COPY lines,
# not by this file. TX-4's rule (the context is only what the Dockerfile
# copies) is lifted for that reason; what it guarded against stays out here:
# the repository's history, any .env (a secret in the context is a secret in
# the test stage), and caches. tests/test_deploy_hardening.py holds this
# list against the Dockerfile and against what the suite reads.
# =============================================================================
.git
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
